  "content": "## Claim\n\nA document model has three parts:\n\n1. **State schema** \u2014 what the document contains\n2. **Action schema** \u2014 what changes are allowed\n3. **Reducer** \u2014 a pure function `(state, action) \u2192 state`\n\n## Runtime behavior\n\nActions are signed expressions of intent. The runtime applies them through the reducer and emits operations (action + ordinal + timestamp + result hash). Replay re-executes the reducer rather than replaying pre-computed domain events.\n\n## Why it fits skills\n\nSkills become thin wrappers that emit allowed actions against declared document models, which makes their contributions attributable and replayable.",
